{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "rule": "no_dropped_step",
 "category": "completeness",
 "family": "no_dropped_step",
 "positiveClass": "fail",
 "definition": "no_dropped_step — a run against the same agent's earlier runs of its own case. The earlier runs read are the 20 most recent, newest first, less any whose calls were not recorded. The rule FAILS when every one of them called a tool that this run never called; look-ups are steps like any other. An explicit empty list of tool calls is a run that made no call and is judged. The rule SKIPS when no tool calls were sent at all; below three earlier runs with recorded calls (insufficient_history); and when no tool was called by every earlier run. A measurement: at the shipped configuration it reports and decides no verdict. Positive = the run dropped a step every earlier run took (the rule should FAIL).",
 "source": "Authored 2026-11-10. Synthetic histories chosen so every label follows from the count stated in the note: all and all but one of the earlier runs at three to twenty of them, the window of twenty, an explicit empty list, runs with no recorded calls, and histories that share no step.",
 "labelling": "Labelled 2026-11-10 against the written definition by counting: each note states how many of the earlier runs called the tool, and the label follows from that count. A conformance family: it measures that the rule does what its definition says, not what a departure is worth, and a case where the rule skips is a negative. What a fire is worth is measured on AgentDojo runs and published in proof/OUTSIDE.md.",
 "labelBasis": "definition",
 "authored": "2026-11-10",
